      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T16:33:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Greg and I were discussing the trade offs of this as a non-virtual call, vs. a virtual call and we do want to keep all of the command handling functions non-virtual but it would be nice to avoid the risk of having an implementer forget to call `transformScissor`.\n\nOne way we came up with that would address this is if we added a `Scissor` struct to `DrawTypes.h` (or maybe `CommandTypes.h`) that stored the scissor rect privately and had a getter function that took in the replay translation and replay clip. The big switch would just forward `fReplayTranslation` and `fReplayClip` into the accessor.\n\nFor convenience I think it makes sense to have the `setScissor()` functions on the command buffers take an `SkIRect`.\n\nWe can also handle `fColorAttachmentSize` and `fReplayClip` automatically by intersecting the replay clip with the color attachment size, or set the replay clip to the color attachment bounds if the replay clip comes in as empty.",
